WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.386
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Tuesday, November third.

2
00:00:04.386 --> 00:00:07.306
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:11.929
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:13.471
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:21.375
Another vessel was struck off northern Oman, and US officials say American forces carried out limited strikes on Iran's Qeshm Island.

6
00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:25.128
Cyclone Murasu has crossed India's Andhra Pradesh coast.

7
00:00:25.128 --> 00:00:29.811
And the US Embassy in Saudi Arabia has warned of possible attacks on airports.

8
00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:32.341
Here's the detail.

9
00:00:32.341 --> 00:00:35.293
Gulf shipping.

10
00:00:35.293 --> 00:00:44.131
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations: late on Sunday, a vessel about nine nautical miles off Oman's northern tip was struck by an unknown projectile, leaving a hole in its side.

11
00:00:44.131 --> 00:00:48.238
The vessel and crew are reported safe, with no environmental impact.

12
00:00:48.238 --> 00:00:53.234
UKMTO published this nearly a day after the incident; reporting can lag.

13
00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.813
The position is on the Gulf of Oman side.

14
00:00:55.813 --> 00:01:03.987
The latest joint maritime threat update rates the Strait of Hormuz severe and the Gulf of Oman moderate; it was issued before this incident.

15
00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:14.069
Separately, Reported, per US officials quoted by several news organizations: American forces struck radar and air defense sites on Qeshm Island on Monday, after Iran's Revolutionary Guard fired on US aircraft.

16
00:01:14.069 --> 00:01:20.226
The officials called the strikes defensive, not a return to major combat.

17
00:01:20.226 --> 00:01:22.324
US Central Command has not commented.

18
00:01:22.324 --> 00:01:28.248
The Revolutionary Guard says it shot down US drones; that is a claim only.

19
00:01:28.248 --> 00:01:38.361
Tueri suggests operators with voyages near the strait review routing against the current assessment, and plan for possible escalation without assuming it.

20
00:01:38.361 --> 00:01:39.303
India.

21
00:01:39.303 --> 00:01:48.117
Confirmed by the India Meteorological Department: Cyclone Murasu crossed the south Andhra Pradesh coast between about three thirty and five thirty a.m.

22
00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:53.452
India time on Tuesday, with winds of one hundred to one hundred ten kilometers per hour.

23
00:01:53.452 --> 00:01:58.710
It has since weakened to a cyclonic storm, and is forecast to weaken further by tonight.

24
00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:07.372
Reported, per Indian media: thousands of trees and hundreds of power poles are down, with power, communications and transport disrupted.

25
00:02:07.372 --> 00:02:13.172
Eight flights were cancelled at one of the state's main airports, and a main coastal rail line is suspended.

26
00:02:13.172 --> 00:02:22.610
Tueri suggests organizations with people in coastal Andhra Pradesh confirm staff welfare, and check road, rail and flight status before any movement today.

27
00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:23.964
Saudi Arabia.

28
00:02:23.964 --> 00:02:33.101
Confirmed: the US Mission in Saudi Arabia issued a security alert on Monday, warning of potential attacks on airports, possible airspace closures, and flight cancellations.

29
00:02:33.101 --> 00:02:34.681
The alert is new.

30
00:02:34.681 --> 00:02:41.336
The ordered departure of some US staff, in place since October twenty-third, is not, and the US travel advisory is unchanged.

31
00:02:41.336 --> 00:02:46.784
Reported, per the Saudi-led coalition: two drones were intercepted over the Riyadh area on Monday.

32
00:02:46.784 --> 00:02:53.983
Yemen's Houthis say they struck Dammam and Jazan airports; that is a claim only.

33
00:02:53.983 --> 00:03:04.876
At about two forty p.m. local time today, Flightradar twenty-four showed about twenty-nine percent of Riyadh flights cancelled, counted on a different base from Monday's, so no trend can be drawn.

34
00:03:04.876 --> 00:03:13.514
Tueri suggests travelers keep flexible plans and confirm each flight with the airline before leaving for the airport.

35
00:03:13.514 --> 00:03:14.979
Operations check.

36
00:03:14.979 --> 00:03:18.894
Borders and health: the US Ebola attestation rule takes effect at eleven fifty-nine p.m.

37
00:03:18.894 --> 00:03:21.757
Eastern tonight.

38
00:03:21.757 --> 00:03:23.512
It was announced in October, and CDC shows no new change.

39
00:03:23.512 --> 00:03:25.860
Travelers who do not attest will be denied boarding.

40
00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:37.685
Nigeria's health portal confirms a pre-boarding declaration for all arrivals; a reported twenty-one day follow-up is not yet confirmed with the authority.

41
00:03:37.685 --> 00:03:46.368
Aviation, reported by Flightradar twenty-four: a Polish airline flight diverted to Warsaw's second airport this morning over a bomb threat, and that airport was then closed.

42
00:03:46.368 --> 00:03:57.012
Infrastructure: NetBlocks measurements showed internet connectivity in Ukraine's Zhytomyr region at about forty-eight percent of normal on Monday night, during Russian strikes on energy sites.

43
00:03:57.012 --> 00:04:01.797
Security, reported per Reuters: Ukraine and Russia both said their air raid alert apps were hacked.

44
00:04:01.797 --> 00:04:11.305
Maritime, reported per Reuters: NATO is sending patrol aircraft and drones to the Black Sea after attacks on cargo ships last month.

45
00:04:11.305 --> 00:04:20.019
Hazards: Britain's Foreign Office updated its Greece advice today for winter weather and flash flooding.

46
00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:21.498
That's today's brief.

47
00:04:21.498 --> 00:04:21.998
Current as of six a.m.

48
00:04:21.998 --> 00:04:24.316
Central, Tuesday.

49
00:04:24.316 --> 00:04:26.742
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

50
00:04:26.742 --> 00:04:31.375
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

51
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:33.771
Check the original source before you act.

52
00:04:33.771 --> 00:04:42.885
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

53
00:04:42.885 --> 00:04:45.605
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

54
00:04:45.605 --> 00:04:46.696
Thanks for listening.
